-- title:
--   Translation is an additive action
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a normed additive commutative group, let $S \subseteq E$ and let $a, b \in E$. Writing $S[x] = \{\,y : y - x \in S\,\} = x + S$, one has
--   $$\bigl(S[a]\bigr)[b] \;=\; S[a+b].$$
--
--   Iterated translation is translation by the sum: the operation $S \mapsto S[x]$ is an action of the additive group of $E$ on subsets of $E$. This is the bookkeeping identity used whenever a cone is moved twice, for instance when its apex is displaced along the axis and then re-based at a new point.
